Dock keystone, rendering: windows tagged "dock" (features/sidedock) render as a
perspective trapezoid with rounded, anti-aliased corners, a warped drop shadow and
frosted blur that follow it.

From sihooleebd/nixos (features/hyprland/trapezoid.patch at 0a7686c, "dock fix",
which added keystone_rounding / keystone_shadow_* / keystone_parallax and fixed
fractional scale), regenerated against this flake's patched Hyprland, with local
changes:
- ksDockKeystone also runs the window box through renderModif, as the surface box
  already is, so the warp stays on the window during workspace slides and zoom.
- The keystone is oriented by the monitor transform (ksOrientToEdge), so its pinned
  edge is the panel's PHYSICAL right edge -- logical bottom at 90 deg -- matching
  features/sidedock, which keeps the dock on that edge through rotation.
- The keystone is applied in the box's UNROTATED frame and the draw's quad transform
  after it (ksDockKeystone: N * conj * N^-1 * B), so the frosted-blur pass -- drawn
  with the monitor's rotation -- warps to the same trapezoid as the window on a
  rotated screen instead of one turned against it.
- The drop shadow is no longer clipped to the window's FLAT box (that left a shadow
  whose inner edge was the straight flat-box edge, not the trapezoid's; the shader's
  own cutout is warped and suffices), and the frosted-blur pass samples the blurred
  framebuffer at each fragment's screen position (ksScreenUV) instead of the flat
  box's UVs, so the blur behind a tilted card is the blur of what is really behind it.
- Cursor parallax (decoration:keystone_parallax, 0 = off) leans cards toward the
  pointer.

Options: decoration:keystone_inset / _shrink / _rounding / _shadow_range /
_shadow_dx / _shadow_dy / _shadow_alpha / _parallax.

